= A Modest Proposal / 一个小小的建议

#html.p[#emph[For preventing the children of poor people in Ireland from being a burden on their parents or country, and for making them beneficial to the publick.]]

#zh[为了使爱尔兰穷人的孩子不再成为父母或国家的负担，并使他们有益于公众。]

#html.p(id: "en-S001")[#text("It is a melancholy object to those, who walk through this great town, or travel in the country, when they see the streets, the roads, and cabbin-doors crowded with beggars of the female sex, followed by three, four, or six children, all in rags, and importuning every passenger for an alms. These mothers, instead of being able to work for their honest livelihood, are forced to employ all their time in stroling to beg sustenance for their helpless infants who, as they grow up, either turn thieves for want of work, or leave their dear native country, to fight for the Pretender in Spain, or sell themselves to the Barbadoes.")]

#zh(id: "S001")[#text("走过这座大城，或者行经乡间的人，看到街道、道路和茅屋门前挤满女乞丐，身后跟着三四个或六个衣衫褴褛的孩子，向每个过路人纠缠乞讨，都会感到悲哀。这些母亲原本应当靠诚实的劳动谋生，却不得不把全部时间用来四处讨要，养活无助的幼儿。孩子们长大后，或因找不到工作而做贼，或离开亲爱的祖国，去西班牙为王位觊觎者打仗，或把自己卖到巴巴多斯。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S002")[#text("I think it is agreed by all parties, that this prodigious number of children in the arms, or on the backs, or at the heels of their mothers, and frequently of their fathers, is in the present deplorable state of the kingdom, a very great additional grievance; and therefore whoever could find out a fair, cheap and easy method of making these children sound and useful members of the commonwealth, would deserve so well of the publick, as to have his statue set up for a preserver of the nation.")]

#zh(id: "S002")[#text("我想，各方都同意：在这个王国目前可悲的处境中，如此多的孩子，被母亲、也常被父亲抱在怀里、背在背上、带在身后，是额外的一项重大祸患。因此，谁若能找出公道、便宜又简便的方法，使这些孩子成为国家健全而有用的成员，就会大大造福公众，理应立一座雕像，纪念这位国家的救星。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S003")[#text("But my intention is very far from being confined to provide only for the children of professed beggars: it is of a much greater extent, and shall take in the whole number of infants at a certain age, who are born of parents in effect as little able to support them, as those who demand our charity in the streets.")]

#zh(id: "S003")[#text("不过，我的意图远不止照顾以乞讨为业者的孩子。我的计划范围大得多：它将涵盖某一年龄的全部幼儿，他们的父母事实上和街头向我们求施舍的人一样，没有能力养活他们。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S004")[#text("As to my own part, having turned my thoughts for many years upon this important subject, and maturely weighed the several schemes of our projectors, I have always found them grossly mistaken in their computation. It is true, a child just dropt from its dam, may be supported by her milk, for a solar year, with little other nourishment: at most not above the value of two shillings, which the mother may certainly get, or the value in scraps, by her lawful occupation of begging; and it is exactly at one year old that I propose to provide for them in such a manner, as, instead of being a charge upon their parents, or the parish, or wanting food and raiment for the rest of their lives, they shall, on the contrary, contribute to the feeding, and partly to the clothing of many thousands.")]

#zh(id: "S004")[#text("就我个人而言，多年来一直思考这个重要问题，并充分权衡过那些筹划者提出的种种方案；我总发现，他们在计算上大错特错。不错，一个刚从母体落地的孩子，可以靠母乳维持一个太阳年，只需少量其他食物，费用至多不超过两个先令。母亲通过合法的乞讨职业，当然能讨得这笔钱，或等值的残羹剩饭。我建议恰恰在孩子满一岁时，为他们作出这样的安排：他们不再成为父母或教区的负担，也不再终身缺衣少食；相反，他们将帮助数以千计的人解决吃饭问题，并部分解决穿衣问题。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S005")[#text("There is likewise another great advantage in my scheme, that it will prevent those voluntary abortions, and that horrid practice of women murdering their bastard children, alas! too frequent among us, sacrificing the poor innocent babes, I doubt, more to avoid the expence than the shame, which would move tears and pity in the most savage and inhuman breast.")]

#zh(id: "S005")[#text("我的方案还有一个重大优点：它能防止自愿堕胎，也能防止妇女杀害私生子这种可怕的行为。唉，这类事在我们中间太常见了！我怀疑，她们牺牲无辜可怜的婴儿，更多是为了避免开销，而不是为了躲避羞耻；即使最野蛮、最不近人情的心，也会因此流泪生怜。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S006")[#text("The number of souls in this kingdom being usually reckoned one million and a half, of these I calculate there may be about two hundred thousand couple, whose wives are breeders; from which number I subtract thirty thousand couple, who are able to maintain their own children, (although I apprehend there cannot be so many under the present distresses of the kingdom) but this being granted, there will remain a hundred and seventy thousand breeders. I again subtract fifty thousand, for those women who miscarry, or whose children die by accident or disease within the year. There only remain a hundred and twenty thousand children of poor parents annually born. The question therefore is, How this number shall be reared and provided for? which, as I have already said, under the present situation of affairs, is utterly impossible by all the methods hitherto proposed. For we can neither employ them in handicraft or agriculture; they neither build houses, (I mean in the country) nor cultivate land: they can very seldom pick up a livelihood by stealing till they arrive at six years old; except where they are of towardly parts, although I confess they learn the rudiments much earlier; during which time they can however be properly looked upon only as probationers; as I have been informed by a principal gentleman in the county of Cavan, who protested to me, that he never knew above one or two instances under the age of six, even in a part of the kingdom so renowned for the quickest proficiency in that art.")]

#zh(id: "S006")[#text("这个王国的人口通常估为一百五十万。我估计其中约有二十万对夫妇，妻子具有生育能力；扣去三万对能自行养育孩子的夫妇——虽然在王国目前的困境下，我担心达不到这个数目，但姑且承认——就剩下十七万名生育者。再扣去五万名流产、或者孩子在一年内因意外或疾病死亡的妇女，每年便只剩下十二万个贫穷父母的孩子出生。问题是，这么多孩子该如何养育、如何供给？正如前面所说，在目前的情况下，迄今提出的一切方法都完全办不到。我们既不能让他们从事手工业，也不能让他们从事农业；他们既不盖房子——我指在乡间——也不种地。不到六岁，他们很少能靠偷窃糊口，除非特别早慧；我承认，他们学习入门本领要早得多，但在这段时间内，顶多只能算见习者。卡文郡一位重要的绅士告诉我，即使在王国中以最快掌握这种技艺而闻名的地区，他也从未听说过六岁以下有超过一两个这样的例子。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S007")[#text("I am assured by our merchants, that a boy or a girl, before twelve years old, is no saleable commodity, and even when they come to this age, they will not yield above three pounds, or three pounds and half a crown at most, on the exchange; which cannot turn to account either to the parents or kingdom, the charge of nutriments and rags having been at least four times that value.")]

#zh(id: "S007")[#text("我们的商人向我保证，男孩或女孩在十二岁之前，都算不上可以出售的商品；即使到了这个年纪，在市场上也卖不到三个英镑以上，至多三个英镑再加半克朗。父母和王国都无法从中获益，因为营养和破衣烂衫的费用，至少已经达到这一价值的四倍。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S008")[#text("I shall now therefore humbly propose my own thoughts, which I hope will not be liable to the least objection.")]

#zh(id: "S008")[#text("因此，我现在恭敬地提出自己的想法，希望它不致遭到丝毫反对。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S009")[#text("I have been assured by a very knowing American of my acquaintance in London, that a young healthy child well nursed, is, at a year old, a most delicious nourishing and wholesome food, whether stewed, roasted, baked, or boiled; and I make no doubt that it will equally serve in a fricasee, or a ragoust.")]

#zh(id: "S009")[#text("我在伦敦认识一位见多识广的美国人，他向我保证：一个年幼、健康、哺养良好的孩子，满一岁时，是最美味、最有营养、最有益健康的食物，无论炖、烤、焙还是煮。我毫不怀疑，用来做白汁炖肉或浓汁杂烩也同样合适。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S010")[#text("I do therefore humbly offer it to publick consideration, that of the hundred and twenty thousand children, already computed, twenty thousand may be reserved for breed, whereof only one fourth part to be males; which is more than we allow to sheep, black cattle, or swine, and my reason is, that these children are seldom the fruits of marriage, a circumstance not much regarded by our savages, therefore, one male will be sufficient to serve four females. That the remaining hundred thousand may, at a year old, be offered in sale to the persons of quality and fortune, through the kingdom, always advising the mother to let them suck plentifully in the last month, so as to render them plump, and fat for a good table. A child will make two dishes at an entertainment for friends, and when the family dines alone, the fore or hind quarter will make a reasonable dish, and seasoned with a little pepper or salt, will be very good boiled on the fourth day, especially in winter.")]

#zh(id: "S010")[#text("因此，我恭敬地建议公众考虑：在已计算出的十二万个孩子中，保留两万个用于繁殖，其中男孩只占四分之一；这已经比我们给羊、牛或猪保留的比例更高。理由是，这些孩子很少是婚姻的产物，我们这里的野蛮人不大在意婚姻，所以一个男性足以供四个女性使用。剩下十万个，可以在满一岁时，在全国卖给有身份、有财产的人。务必劝母亲在最后一个月让他们尽量多吃母乳，使他们长得肥胖，配得上一张好餐桌。一个孩子足够做两道菜，用来招待朋友；若只是自家用餐，前四分之一或后四分之一就足够成为一道像样的菜。撒一点胡椒或盐，即使到第四天再煮，也会十分可口，尤其在冬天。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S011")[#text("I have reckoned upon a medium, that a child just born will weigh 12 pounds, and in a solar year, if tolerably nursed, encreaseth to 28 pounds.")]

#zh(id: "S011")[#text("我计算的平均数是，孩子出生时重12磅，只要照料尚可，一个太阳年后就会长到28磅。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S012")[#text("I grant this food will be somewhat dear, and therefore very proper for landlords, who, as they have already devoured most of the parents, seem to have the best title to the children.")]

#zh(id: "S012")[#text("我承认，这种食物会有些昂贵，因此特别适合地主。他们既然已经吞噬了大多数父母，似乎也最有资格占有孩子。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S013")[#text("Infant’s flesh will be in season throughout the year, but more plentiful in March, and a little before and after; for we are told by a grave author, an eminent French physician, that fish being a prolifick dyet, there are more children born in Roman Catholick countries about nine months after Lent, than at any other season; therefore, reckoning a year after Lent, the markets will be more glutted than usual, because the number of Popish infants, is at least three to one in this kingdom, and therefore it will have one other collateral advantage, by lessening the number of Papists among us.")]

#zh(id: "S013")[#text("婴儿肉一年四季都可以上市，但在三月以及前后的一段时间会更多。一位严肃的作者、著名的法国医生告诉我们，鱼是一种有助繁殖的食物，因此在天主教国家，四旬斋过后约九个月，出生的孩子比其他季节更多。于是，算到四旬斋一年以后，市场便会比平常更充裕；因为在这个王国，天主教婴儿与其他婴儿的数量至少是三比一。所以，这还会带来另一项附带的优点：减少我们中间天主教徒的人数。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S014")[#text("I have already computed the charge of nursing a beggar’s child (in which list I reckon all cottagers, labourers, and four-fifths of the farmers) to be about two shillings per annum, rags included; and I believe no gentleman would repine to give ten shillings for the carcass of a good fat child, which, as I have said, will make four dishes of excellent nutritive meat, when he hath only some particular friend, or his own family to dine with him. Thus the squire will learn to be a good landlord, and grow popular among his tenants, the mother will have eight shillings neat profit, and be fit for work till she produces another child.")]

#zh(id: "S014")[#text("我已经算过，养育一个乞丐的孩子——在这个名单中，我把所有茅屋居民、劳工和五分之四的农民都算进去——连破衣服在内，每年大约要两个先令。我相信，没有哪位绅士会舍不得花十个先令，买一个健康肥胖孩子的胴体。正如我说过的，当他只招待一位特别的朋友，或者只与自家人用餐时，这足够做四道营养上佳的肉菜。这样，乡绅就会学着成为一个好地主，受到佃户的欢迎；母亲则有八个先令的净利，而且在生下另一个孩子之前，都可以工作。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S015")[#text("Those who are more thrifty (as I must confess the times require) may flay the carcass; the skin of which, artificially dressed, will make admirable gloves for ladies, and summer boots for fine gentlemen.")]

#zh(id: "S015")[#text("更加节俭的人——我必须承认，时势要求如此——还可以剥下胴体的皮。经过精心鞣制，皮可以为女士制作极好的手套，为体面的绅士制作夏靴。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S016")[#text("As to our City of Dublin, shambles may be appointed for this purpose, in the most convenient parts of it, and butchers we may be assured will not be wanting; although I rather recommend buying the children alive, and dressing them hot from the knife, as we do roasting pigs.")]

#zh(id: "S016")[#text("在我们的都柏林城，可以在最便利的地方设立专用屠宰场；我们可以放心，屠夫不会短缺。不过，我更建议买活孩子，像处理烤乳猪一样，刚下刀就趁热料理。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S017")[#text("A very worthy person, a true lover of his country, and whose virtues I highly esteem, was lately pleased in discoursing on this matter, to offer a refinement upon my scheme. He said, that many gentlemen of this kingdom, having of late destroyed their deer, he conceived that the want of venison might be well supplied by the bodies of young lads and maidens, not exceeding fourteen years of age, nor under twelve; so great a number of both sexes in every county being now ready to starve for want of work and service: and these to be disposed of by their parents if alive, or otherwise by their nearest relations. But with due deference to so excellent a friend, and so deserving a patriot, I cannot be altogether in his sentiments; for as to the males, my American acquaintance assured me from frequent experience, that their flesh was generally tough and lean, like that of our schoolboys, by continual exercise, and their taste disagreeable, and to fatten them would not answer the charge. Then as to the females, it would, I think, with humble submission, be a loss to the publick, because they soon would become breeders themselves: and besides, it is not improbable that some scrupulous people might be apt to censure such a practice, (although indeed very unjustly) as a little bordering upon cruelty, which, I confess, hath always been with me the strongest objection against any project, how well soever intended.")]

#zh(id: "S017")[#text("一位非常值得尊敬的人，真正热爱祖国，我也十分敬重他的美德。最近谈论此事时，他欣然为我的方案提出一项改进。他说，王国里许多绅士近来已经杀光了自己的鹿，因此，缺少的鹿肉，可以用十二岁至十四岁之间的少男少女的身体很好地补充。现在每个郡都有大量这样的男女，因找不到工作、无人雇用而即将饿死。父母若还活着，就由父母处置他们，否则由最近的亲属处置。然而，尽管我充分尊重这位优秀的朋友和值得敬重的爱国者，却不能完全同意。说到男孩，我那位美国熟人依据丰富的经验告诉我，他们常年活动，肉通常又韧又瘦，像我们的学童一样，味道也不好；把他们养肥又不值得花那笔钱。至于女孩，恕我冒昧，我认为这会使公众蒙受损失，因为她们很快就能自己成为生育者。此外，一些顾虑较多的人也很可能批评这种做法——当然，这是非常不公正的——认为它有一点接近残酷。我承认，无论一种计划的用意多好，这始终是我反对它时最强烈的理由。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S018")[#text("But in order to justify my friend, he confessed, that this expedient was put into his head by the famous Psalmanaazor, a native of the island Formosa, who came from thence to London, above twenty years ago, and in conversation told my friend, that in his country, when any young person happened to be put to death, the executioner sold the carcass to persons of quality, as a prime dainty; and that, in his time, the body of a plump girl of fifteen, who was crucified for an attempt to poison the Emperor, was sold to his imperial majesty’s prime minister of state, and other great mandarins of the court in joints from the gibbet, at four hundred crowns. Neither indeed can I deny, that if the same use were made of several plump young girls in this town, who without one single groat to their fortunes, cannot stir abroad without a chair, and appear at a playhouse and assemblies in foreign fineries which they never will pay for, the kingdom would not be the worse.")]

#zh(id: "S018")[#text("不过，为了替我的朋友辩护，他承认，这个办法是著名的萨尔马纳扎尔让他想到的。此人自称是福尔摩沙岛人，二十多年前从那里来到伦敦，交谈时告诉我朋友：在他的国家，年轻人一旦被处死，刽子手就把胴体卖给有身份的人，作为珍贵的美味。他在世时，一个十五岁的胖姑娘因企图毒死皇帝而被钉死，她的身体从刑架上分割下来，以四百克朗的价格，卖给皇帝的首相和宫廷其他大官。事实上，我也不能否认，如果同样利用本城一些丰腴的年轻姑娘，王国并不会变得更坏。她们虽然没有一个格罗特的财产，出门却非坐轿子不可；去剧院或聚会时，还穿着永远不会付款的外国华服。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S019")[#text("Some persons of a desponding spirit are in great concern about that vast number of poor people, who are aged, diseased, or maimed; and I have been desired to employ my thoughts what course may be taken, to ease the nation of so grievous an incumbrance. But I am not in the least pain upon that matter, because it is very well known, that they are every day dying, and rotting, by cold and famine, and filth, and vermin, as fast as can be reasonably expected. And as to the young labourers, they are now in almost as hopeful a condition. They cannot get work, and consequently pine away from want of nourishment, to a degree, that if at any time they are accidentally hired to common labour, they have not strength to perform it, and thus the country and themselves are happily delivered from the evils to come.")]

#zh(id: "S019")[#text("有些悲观的人非常担心那些年老、患病或残疾的众多穷人。他们要求我思考，有什么办法能使国家卸下如此沉重的负担。不过，我对此丝毫不忧虑，因为大家都知道，他们每天都因寒冷、饥饿、污秽和虫害而死去、腐烂，速度已快到可以合理预期的程度。至于年轻劳工，他们现在的处境也差不多同样有希望。他们找不到工作，因而营养不足，日渐衰弱；到了某一天偶然被雇去做普通劳动，也已没有力气完成，于是国家和他们本人，都幸而免除了将来的祸患。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S020")[#text("I have too long digressed, and therefore shall return to my subject. I think the advantages by the proposal which I have made are obvious and many, as well as of the highest importance.")]

#zh(id: "S020")[#text("我离题已经太久，现在回到正题。我认为，这个建议的优点显而易见，数量很多，而且极其重要。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S021")[#text("For first, as I have already observed, it would greatly lessen the number of Papists, with whom we are yearly overrun, being the principal breeders of the nation, as well as our most dangerous enemies, and who stay at home on purpose with a design to deliver the kingdom to the Pretender, hoping to take their advantage by the absence of so many good Protestants, who have chosen rather to leave their country, than stay at home and pay tithes against their conscience to an episcopal curate.")]

#zh(id: "S021")[#text("第一，正如我已经指出的，它将大大减少天主教徒的人数。他们是国家主要的生育者，也是我们最危险的敌人，每年都多得使我们难以承受。他们故意留在国内，企图把王国交给王位觊觎者，指望利用许多优秀的新教徒离国的机会；那些新教徒宁愿离开祖国，也不肯违背良心，留在国内向主教制教会的牧师缴纳什一税。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S022")[#text("Secondly, The poorer tenants will have something valuable of their own, which by law may be made liable to a distress, and help to pay their landlord’s rent, their corn and cattle being already seized, and money a thing unknown.")]

#zh(id: "S022")[#text("第二，贫穷的佃户将拥有某种属于自己的有价值的东西；法律可以把它作为抵债的财产，用来帮助支付地主的租金。他们的粮食和牲畜早已被扣押，至于金钱，他们连见都没见过。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S023")[#text("Thirdly, Whereas the maintainance of a hundred thousand children, from two years old, and upwards, cannot be computed at less than ten shillings a piece per annum, the nation’s stock will be thereby encreased fifty thousand pounds per annum, besides the profit of a new dish, introduced to the tables of all gentlemen of fortune in the kingdom, who have any refinement in taste. And the money will circulate among our selves, the goods being entirely of our own growth and manufacture.")]

#zh(id: "S023")[#text("第三，供养十万个两岁以上的孩子，每个每年至少要花十个先令；这样，国家的财富每年便可增加五万英镑。此外，还能使全国所有有财产、有一点饮食品位的绅士，餐桌上多一道新菜，获得另一项利益。这些钱也将在我们自己人之间流通，因为商品完全由本国繁育、制造。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S024")[#text("Fourthly, The constant breeders, besides the gain of eight shillings sterling per annum by the sale of their children, will be rid of the charge of maintaining them after the first year.")]

#zh(id: "S024")[#text("第四，那些不断生育的人，除了每年卖孩子所得的八个先令英币，还能免去孩子满一岁以后的抚养费用。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S025")[#text("Fifthly, This food would likewise bring great custom to taverns, where the vintners will certainly be so prudent as to procure the best receipts for dressing it to perfection; and consequently have their houses frequented by all the fine gentlemen, who justly value themselves upon their knowledge in good eating; and a skilful cook, who understands how to oblige his guests, will contrive to make it as expensive as they please.")]

#zh(id: "S025")[#text("第五，这种食物还会给酒馆带来很多生意。酒馆老板自然会明智地寻求最好的烹调配方，使它达到完美，于是那些以精通美食为荣、也确实值得如此自负的体面绅士，都会经常光顾。懂得取悦客人的高明厨师，则会设法把价格抬到客人愿意接受的任何高度。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S026")[#text("Sixthly, This would be a great inducement to marriage, which all wise nations have either encouraged by rewards, or enforced by laws and penalties. It would encrease the care and tenderness of mothers towards their children, when they were sure of a settlement for life to the poor babes, provided in some sort by the publick, to their annual profit instead of expence. We should soon see an honest emulation among the married women, which of them could bring the fattest child to the market. Men would become as fond of their wives, during the time of their pregnancy, as they are now of their mares in foal, their cows in calf, or sows when they are ready to farrow; nor offer to beat or kick them (as is too frequent a practice) for fear of a miscarriage.")]

#zh(id: "S026")[#text("第六，这将强烈促进婚姻。所有明智的国家，都曾用奖赏鼓励婚姻，或者用法律与惩罚强制婚姻。母亲一旦确信，公众已经在某种程度上替可怜的婴儿安排了终身归宿，使她们每年得到收益而不再花钱，就会对孩子更加关心、更加温柔。我们很快就会看到，已婚妇女之间展开诚实的竞争，比谁能把最肥胖的孩子带到市场。男人在妻子怀孕期间，将会像现在对待怀驹的母马、怀犊的母牛和即将产仔的母猪一样珍爱她们；也不会再打她们或踢她们——这种事现在太常见了——因为害怕造成流产。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S027")[#text("Many other advantages might be enumerated. For instance, the addition of some thousand carcasses in our exportation of barrel’d beef: the propagation of swine’s flesh, and improvement in the art of making good bacon, so much wanted among us by the great destruction of pigs, too frequent at our tables; which are no way comparable in taste or magnificence to a well grown, fat yearling child, which roasted whole will make a considerable figure at a Lord Mayor’s feast, or any other publick entertainment. But this, and many others, I omit, being studious of brevity.")]

#zh(id: "S027")[#text("还可以列举很多其他优点。例如，我们出口的桶装牛肉可以多添几千具胴体；猪肉生产可以扩大，腌制上好咸肉的技艺可以改进。我们这里特别缺少这些，因为餐桌上太频繁地大量吃掉猪肉。然而，无论味道还是气派，猪肉都无法与一个长得结实肥胖的一岁孩子相比；整只烤好后，它在市长的宴席或任何其他公开宴会上，都会十分壮观。不过，为求简短，这些以及许多其他优点，我就不谈了。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S028")[#text("Supposing that one thousand families in this city, would be constant customers for infants flesh, besides others who might have it at merry meetings, particularly at weddings and christenings, I compute that Dublin would take off annually about twenty thousand carcasses; and the rest of the kingdom (where probably they will be sold somewhat cheaper) the remaining eighty thousand.")]

#zh(id: "S028")[#text("假设本城有一千户家庭，会成为婴儿肉的固定顾客，此外，还有其他人会在欢乐聚会，尤其是婚礼和洗礼宴会上享用，那么我估计，都柏林每年将消耗大约两万具胴体；王国其余地区——在那里大概会卖得稍便宜些——将消耗剩下的八万具。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S029")[#text("I can think of no one objection, that will possibly be raised against this proposal, unless it should be urged, that the number of people will be thereby much lessened in the kingdom. This I freely own, and was indeed one principal design in offering it to the world. I desire the reader will observe, that I calculate my remedy for this one individual Kingdom of Ireland, and for no other that ever was, is, or, I think, ever can be upon Earth. Therefore let no man talk to me of other expedients: Of taxing our absentees at five shillings a pound: Of using neither clothes, nor houshold furniture, except what is of our own growth and manufacture: Of utterly rejecting the materials and instruments that promote foreign luxury: Of curing the expensiveness of pride, vanity, idleness, and gaming in our women: Of introducing a vein of parsimony, prudence and temperance: Of learning to love our country, wherein we differ even from Laplanders, and the inhabitants of Topinamboo: Of quitting our animosities and factions, nor acting any longer like the Jews, who were murdering one another at the very moment their city was taken: Of being a little cautious not to sell our country and consciences for nothing: Of teaching landlords to have at least one degree of mercy towards their tenants. Lastly, of putting a spirit of honesty, industry, and skill into our shopkeepers, who, if a resolution could now be taken to buy only our native goods, would immediately unite to cheat and exact upon us in the price, the measure, and the goodness, nor could ever yet be brought to make one fair proposal of just dealing, though often and earnestly invited to it.")]

#zh(id: "S029")[#text("我想不出这个建议可能遭到什么反对，除非有人说，它会使王国的人口大大减少。这一点我坦然承认，而且正是我把建议公诸世间的主要目的之一。请读者注意，我开出的药方，只针对爱尔兰这一个王国，不针对地球上过去、现在，或者依我看将来可能存在的任何其他国家。因此，请不要跟我谈别的办法：向不住在本国的地主，每英镑收入征收五个先令；除本国生长、制造的衣服和家具外，一概不用；彻底拒绝助长外国奢侈风气的材料和工具；医治妇女因骄傲、虚荣、懒惰和赌博而养成的挥霍；培养节俭、审慎和节制的风气；学会爱自己的国家——在这一点上，我们甚至不如拉普兰人和图皮南布人；放下敌意和派系之争，不再像城池被攻占的那一刻还在互相残杀的犹太人；稍加小心，不把祖国和良心白白卖掉；教地主至少对佃户怀有一点仁慈。最后，让我们的店主具有诚实、勤劳和技艺的精神。因为，即使我们现在决定只购买国货，他们也会马上联合起来，在价格、分量和质量上欺骗我们、勒索我们；尽管我们屡次真诚邀请，他们至今却从未提出过一项公平交易的合理建议。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S030")[#text("Therefore I repeat, let no man talk to me of these and the like expedients, till he hath at least some glympse of hope, that there will ever be some hearty and sincere attempt to put them into practice.")]

#zh(id: "S030")[#text("因此，我再说一次：在还没有哪怕一线希望，表明人们将会真心诚意地尝试实施这些措施之前，请不要跟我谈这些或类似的办法。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S031")[#text("But, as to myself, having been wearied out for many years with offering vain, idle, visionary thoughts, and at length utterly despairing of success, I fortunately fell upon this proposal, which, as it is wholly new, so it hath something solid and real, of no expence and little trouble, full in our own power, and whereby we can incur no danger in disobliging England. For this kind of commodity will not bear exportation, and flesh being of too tender a consistence, to admit a long continuance in salt, although perhaps I could name a country, which would be glad to eat up our whole nation without it.")]

#zh(id: "S031")[#text("至于我自己，多年来不断提出徒劳、无用、空想的念头，早已疲惫不堪，最后对成功彻底绝望；幸而想到了这个建议。它完全新颖，又切实可靠，不需花费，也不大费事，完全在我们自己的能力范围之内，而且不会冒着得罪英国的危险。因为这种商品经不起出口，肉质太嫩，无法长期腌存；不过，也许我倒能说出一个国家的名字，它不必腌盐，就很乐意把我们整个民族吞下去。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S032")[#text("After all, I am not so violently bent upon my own opinion, as to reject any offer, proposed by wise men, which shall be found equally innocent, cheap, easy, and effectual. But before something of that kind shall be advanced in contradiction to my scheme, and offering a better, I desire the author or authors will be pleased maturely to consider two points. First, As things now stand, how they will be able to find food and raiment for a hundred thousand useless mouths and backs. And secondly, There being a round million of creatures in humane figure throughout this kingdom, whose whole subsistence put into a common stock, would leave them in debt two million of pounds sterling, adding those who are beggars by profession, to the bulk of farmers, cottagers and labourers, with their wives and children, who are beggars in effect; I desire those politicians who dislike my overture, and may perhaps be so bold to attempt an answer, that they will first ask the parents of these mortals, whether they would not at this day think it a great happiness to have been sold for food at a year old, in the manner I prescribe, and thereby have avoided such a perpetual scene of misfortunes, as they have since gone through, by the oppression of landlords, the impossibility of paying rent without money or trade, the want of common sustenance, with neither house nor clothes to cover them from the inclemencies of the weather, and the most inevitable prospect of intailing the like, or greater miseries, upon their breed for ever.")]

#zh(id: "S032")[#text("总之，我并没有顽固到只肯坚持自己的意见，拒绝任何聪明人提出的同样无害、便宜、简便而有效的建议。不过，在拿出某种这样的方案来反对我的计划，并声称它更好之前，请作者或作者们充分考虑两点。第一，在目前的情况下，他们怎样为十万张无用的嘴和十万个无用的身体找到食物和衣服？第二，这个王国里有整整一百万个具有人形的生灵；把他们所有的生计收入合在一起，仍会负债两百万英镑。其中既包括以乞讨为业的人，也包括实际上已经是乞丐的大部分农民、茅屋居民、劳工，以及他们的妻子和孩子。那些不喜欢我的提议，也许还敢尝试回答的政治家，请先问问这些人的父母：如果自己在一岁时，就按我规定的方式被卖作食物，他们今天难道不认为那是一种莫大的幸福吗？这样便可以免去此后没完没了的灾难：地主的压迫，没有钱和生意却必须付租的困境，基本食物的缺乏，没有房子和衣服来遮挡恶劣天气，以及几乎无法避免的前景——把同样、甚至更大的苦难，永久传给自己的后代。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S033")[#text("I profess in the sincerity of my heart, that I have not the least personal interest in endeavouring to promote this necessary work, having no other motive than the publick good of my country, by advancing our trade, providing for infants, relieving the poor, and giving some pleasure to the rich. I have no children, by which I can propose to get a single penny; the youngest being nine years old, and my wife past child-bearing.")]

#zh(id: "S033")[#text("我由衷声明：在努力推进这项必要的工作时，我没有丝毫个人利益。我的唯一动机，是通过发展贸易、安置婴儿、救济穷人，并给富人一点乐趣，增进祖国的公共利益。我没有可以使自己从中赚到一个便士的孩子：最小的已经九岁，妻子也过了生育的年龄。")]
